# Castlevania: Curse of Darkness (4B4E002D), FIRST RUN: no save on the disk.
# PLAYED by nav.py on the Nova, 2026-10-01 14:18 PDT (lane.titleroutes HELD
# session castlevania-cod.first-run-20261001T141851, the owner-approved
# one-time Nova path-finding session, #397).
#
# Replaces the two earlier drafts, neither ever played past a menu:
# lane.routeprep's all-[guess] draft (adopted session 42, never replayed) and
# the generic `--route survey`-derived castlevania-cod.route (session 48,
# Thor, heat-stopped at 284/300s, never confirmed by a real replay). The
# trap both missed: NEW GAME's Name Entry keyboard needs an explicit jump to
# "Accept" (press START, which jumps the cursor there on this keyboard; A
# alone leaves the cursor on the letter grid), and the save-data prompt
# right after defaults its cursor to "No" (axis LX min moves it onto "Yes"
# before A, or the route declines its own save and loops back to Name
# Entry).
#
#   intro FMV (A) -> title, New Game (A) -> Name Entry: A types the
#   highlighted "A", START jumps the cursor to Accept, A accepts -> "Is this
#   correct?" (A, Yes already selected) -> "There is no save data... Create
#   new save data?" (LX min moves the cursor from the default No onto Yes,
#   then A) -> "Creating new save data..." -> save slot list, slot 1
#   highlighted (A) -> "Saving..." -> the opening cutscene (1476, Valachia;
#   A three times, 5.4s apart, clears the castle-exterior shots) -> player
#   control in a gothic courtyard facing a gargoyle fountain.
#
# Player control confirmed by eye: LY min visibly closed the distance to the
# fountain between two shots taken 1.5s apart (014-moved.png), then the play
# pattern (LY min/press A/RX sweep) walked him along the fountain's edge and
# into an attack animation (016-postplay.png). HP bar steady at 100/100
# throughout -- no combat pressure this early.
#
# REPLAYED UNATTENDED, FAILED (session 59, #397, dispatch request
# 1790902028-titleroutes-1005086, Nova): the "press A, wait 1.1, shot
# name-a" step that is supposed to type the highlighted letter "A" into
# the name field fired before the Name Entry screen was interactive -- the
# field in 174838-name-a.png is still empty, unlike the interactive nav.py
# session's own 003-name-a.png (field shows "A" typed) from the identical
# command/timing sequence. Every frame after that (accepted/yes/left1/
# createdsave/wait5/slot1/saved1/a2/a5/gameplay) is the SAME Name Entry
# screen with an empty name forever -- Accept silently refuses an empty
# name, so the whole rest of the route (save creation, cutscene, the
# `mark gameplay` itself) never happened; the registry's stored save for
# 4B4E002D was unchanged by this run (still 53f0a40fe626, no save slot).
# This is a timing race in the newgame->Name-Entry transition, not a step
# ordering bug (the same fixed-wait sequence worked once, by eye, in the
# interactive session that authored this route). Fixed by making the
# letter-type step self-healing: press A on the "A" tile twice, a few
# seconds apart. The cursor does not move off the "A" tile after a
# successful type (confirmed in 003-name-a.png), so a redundant second
# press just yields "AA" instead of "A" if the first one landed, and
# recovers a dropped first press if it didn't -- either way the name is
# non-empty by the time START jumps to Accept. NOT YET REPLAYED with this
# fix: treat as a draft until a soak or scratch/replay.sh run confirms it
# reaches real gameplay and creates a save.
wait 10.9
shot boot
wait 13.4
press A
wait 5.8
shot a1
wait 10.3
press A
wait 3.1
shot newgame
wait 14
press A
wait 1.1
shot name-a
wait 4
press A
wait 1.1
shot name-a2
wait 4.1
press START
wait 1.1
shot name-start
wait 7.6
press A
wait 2.1
shot accepted
wait 6.7
press A
wait 3.1
shot yes
wait 11.2
axis LX min
wait 0.5
axis LX mid
wait 1.1
shot left1
wait 8.5
press A
wait 4.1
shot createdsave
wait 12.1
shot wait5
wait 8.3
press A
wait 4.1
shot slot1
wait 13.4
shot saved1
wait 18.7
press A
wait 5.1
shot a2
wait 7.5
press A
wait 5.4
press A
wait 5.4
press A
wait 5.7
shot a5
wait 9.0
axis LY min
wait 1.7
axis LY mid
shot moved
wait 7.2
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 2
    press A
    axis RX max
    wait 0.5
    axis RX mid
    axis LY mid
    wait 1
    press A
    wait 2
}
